%U A105595 27,19,39,1,1,3,1,5,5,3,9,3,5,11,9,9,13,19,21,3,7,7,9,7,15,17,19,7,15,21
%N A105595 Row sums of number triangle A105594.
%C A105595 Conjecture : all terms are odd.
%C A105595 Every term is odd. Proof: Work modulo 2 and put s_j = abs(mu(binomial(n,j))). By the definition of A105594, T(n,k) = Sum_{j=0..n} s_j*binomial(j,k) (mod 2). Hence the parity of the n-th row sum is Sum_{k=0..n} T(n,k) = Sum_{j=0..n} s_j*Sum_{k=0..j} binomial(j,k) = Sum_{j=0..n} s_j*2^j = s_0 = 1 (mod 2), because s_0 = abs(mu(1)) = 1. Thus every term of A105595 is odd. - _Bing Gao_, Sep 22 2026
%F A105595 a(n) = Sum_{k=0..n} mod(Sum_{j=0..n} abs(mu(binomial(n, j)))*mod(binomial(j, k), 2), 2).
%p A105595 A105595 := proc(n)
%p A105595     add(A105594(n,k),k=0..n) ;
%p A105595 end proc: # _R. J. Mathar_, Nov 28 2014
